{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>On the breastplate.</b> For the needs of the breastplate — to set them in it. And it is not tenable to say that their initial making was upon it, for if so, what is he going back and saying ״וְנָתַתָ אֶת שְׁתֵּי הַטַּבָּעוֹת״ — are they not already set in it? He should have written at the beginning of the verse ״וְעָשִׂיתָ עַל קְצוֹת הַחֹשֶׁן שְׁתֵּי טַבְּעוֹת זָהָב״ — and with the chains too you must interpret likewise." "<b>On the two ends of the breastplate.</b> The two edges opposite the neck, right and left, which come against the shoulder-pieces of the ephod."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:15.499085114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}